cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use sciwrite-lint in your research, please cite the paper below."
type: software
title: sciwrite-lint
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-04-28"
abstract: >
  A linter for scientific manuscripts. Verifies that cited references exist
  and have accurate metadata, downloads cited papers and checks whether they
  actually support the claims made, analyzes figures against their captions,
  flags cross-section inconsistencies, and batch-checks the bibliographies of
  cited papers. Runs entirely on the user's machine via local vLLM —
  manuscript text never leaves the local machine; only citation metadata
  is sent to verification APIs. Produces a SciLint Score.
authors:
  - family-names: Samsonau
    given-names: Sergey V.
url: "https://github.com/authentic-research-partners/sciwrite-lint"
repository-code: "https://github.com/authentic-research-partners/sciwrite-lint"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - linter
  - latex
  - bibtex
  - scientific-writing
  - academic-writing
  - citation-checker
  - reference-verification
  - claim-verification
  - manuscript
  - peer-review
  - arxiv
  - vllm
  - qwen
